Design for Active Disassembly strategy uses smart materials or structure to activate product disassembly. Usually, a process of this is activated when the product is heated, microwaved or through variations in ambient pressure. This strategy is used to decrease the time needed for disassembling and implies the use of technology and smart materials. The amount of links that can be unmounted at the same time for one disassembly operation is unlimited. 

Designers should attempt to:
• Use compatible materials;
• Group harmful materials into subassemblies;
• Avoid ageing and corrosive material combination;
• Protect subassemblies against soiling and corrosion;
• Avoid metal inserts in plastic parts;
• Use standard subassemblies and parts;
• Minimize the number of fastener types; 
• Limitation to the number of different materials; 
• Standardize parts for multiple uses;
• Limit material variability;